From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:49:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix solo GBA detection (shader mode) and joiner controls
 (auto-map)

Two device-confirmed bugs, both Android weak-point issues:

1. Solo detection regressed in v0.4.29 because the XD graphics preset set
   ShaderCompilationMode=0 (synchronous specialized). On a cold Adreno
   shader cache, synchronous pipeline compiles on the GC video thread hold
   the shared Vulkan queue and back-pressure the GBA core's frame callback
   (the code already warns the event thread 'can stall in the synchronous
   frame callback'), starving Emerald's link-init frames so the joybus
   handshake never latches -- telemetry: win/rst/prb climbing, est=0. It was
   never the cheats or the BIOS. Switch to ShaderCompilationMode=3
   (async-skip): still no ubershaders, so the Adreno DEVICE_LOST crash stays
   fixed, but shaders compile in the background so the GBA is never starved.

2. The Android auto-mapper mapped GBA pads 1 and 2 but not pad 0, and a
   netplay joiner's local GBA is pad 0 -- so the joiner's physical buttons
   did nothing and only touch worked. Map all four pads.
---
 Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini                          | 8 +++++++-
 .../dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/input/AutoMapper.kt     | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
index f0e9c182ad..0cf4d9f184 100644
--- a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
+++ b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
@@ -52,7 +52,13 @@ $60 FPS
 # shaders + pre-warming the cache avoid that entirely; native resolution
 # and CPU-side culling give thermal/submission headroom. None of these
 # affect netplay determinism.
-ShaderCompilationMode = 0
+# Async-skip (3), not synchronous specialized (0): specialized shaders (no
+# ubershaders) keep the Adreno DEVICE_LOST watchdog crash fixed, but compiling
+# them SYNCHRONOUSLY on a cold cache holds the shared Vulkan queue and
+# back-pressures the GBA core's frame callback -- starving Emerald's link-init
+# frames so XD never detects the GBA. Async-skip compiles in the background
+# (brief visual pop-in on first use) and never stalls the GBA. Fixes both.
+ShaderCompilationMode = 3
 WaitForShadersBeforeStarting = True
 InternalResolution = 1
 CPUCull = True
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/input/AutoMapper.kt b/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/input/AutoMapper.kt
index 762a9b3c33..acfdda05b2 100644
--- a/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/input/AutoMapper.kt
+++ b/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/input/AutoMapper.kt
@@ -120,7 +120,11 @@ object AutoMapper {
      */
     fun autoMap(): Boolean {
         val gcPad = EmulatedController.getGcPad(0)
-        val gbaPads = listOf(EmulatedController.getGbaPad(1), EmulatedController.getGbaPad(2))
+        // Map ALL four GBA pads, not just 1 and 2. In netplay the JOINER's local
+        // GBA is pad index 0, which was left unmapped -- so the joiner's physical
+        // buttons reached nothing and only on-screen touch worked. Mapping the
+        // unused pads is harmless (only the active local GBA's input is read).
+        val gbaPads = (0..3).map { EmulatedController.getGbaPad(it) }
 
         val gcNeedsMapping = !isControllerMapped(gcPad)
         val gbaNeedingMapping = gbaPads.filterNot { isControllerMapped(it) }
